Spec: TenantReconfigureCmd

Purpose:
  Out of the build graph — this file is dead: ./mod.rs keeps `//mod reconfigure;`, the
    @Commands::Reconfigure variant and the exit-6 arm all commented (frozen in
    ./mod.sdd), so nothing here ever compiles, cargo never tests it, and it is
    unreachable from clap. Everything below is the PROPOSAL frozen verbatim from the
    source, labelled as such — live behaviour only "if reconnected".
  If reconnected, back the tenant lane of `agent tenant reconfigure`: resolve one
    @TenantInstance by namespace and name, publish it as the process-wide owner
    context and as the Rhai variable `instance`, inject the parsed CLI flags as
    `args`, then hand off in order to the Rhai modules `context` and `reconfigure`.
    This file runs no reconfigure stage itself and writes no `status` — engine prep
    and handoff only.
  Diff-verified against the dead twin ./../service/reconfigure.rs: exactly two hunks
    differ. Line 1: the @use line (@set_tenant/@TenantInstance over
    @set_service/@ServiceInstance). Hunk `@@ -78`: the four `format!` sites at lines
    81–84 drop `.display()` and rename the `{script_dir}/service` segment to
    `{script_dir}/tenant`, and lines 86–87 swap @ServiceInstance::get/@set_service
    for @TenantInstance::get/@set_tenant. The ten-flag block, the derives, the
    `args` @unwrap error channel and the four-statement snippet are byte-identical.
  The dropped `.display()` calls are not cosmetic: this copy does NOT compile as
    written while the twin does — see `[?]` Tasks; every entry below assumes the
    frozen proposal is revived with that repaired.

Structure:
  ./reconfigure.rs: dead source, compiled only if the commented triplet in ./mod.rs
    is uncommented per ./mod.sdd — and it then fails the build as-is (Tasks)

References:
  ./mod.sdd — owns the freeze: commented `//mod reconfigure;`, the
    @Commands::Reconfigure variant and the exit-6 error lane
    `Reconfiguring of a package failed with: {e:}` that would drive this file.
  ./../service/reconfigure.sdd — the dead twin; shared flag, JSON and handoff
    contracts plus the sibling revive-or-delete decision (read-only comparison).
  ./install.sdd — tenant shape ancestor: same ten flags and step order except the
    two instance-flag doc words, the `args` injection lane (@unwrap here,
    @map_err + `?` there) and the snippet's last import.
  /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.rs — package entry-point pattern
    `reconfigure.rhai`, the contract revival would have to satisfy.

Depends on:
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Script::new resolver-directory semantics and full
    registration set (new_core plus http, s3, the three instance kinds with
    @tenant_rhai_register, jukebox, k8s registrars), @Script::eval error lane, and
    @Script::set_dynamic / @Script::ctx reached through @std::ops::Deref onto the
    core engine @Script.
  /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — @TenantInstance and the awaited
    @TenantInstance::get lookup, attached by @impl_instance_common!
    (/common/src/instance_macros.sdd): one namespaced named read, client via
    @get_client_async, kube failures wrapped as @common::Error::KubeError.
  /common/src/context.sdd — @set_tenant store semantics and runtime preconditions
    (@tokio::task::block_in_place needs a multi-thread runtime).
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Result, @common::Error variants and
    @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE as the `agent_image` clap default,
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`.
  @clap @Args, @serde, @serde_json — flag parsing and the derives behind the `args`
    JSON.
  ./mod.rs — the sole caller, commented: the awaited call and exit-6
    `unwrap_or_else` lane.
  /agent/scripts/tenant/context.rhai — resolvable handoff script under the default
    `--script-dir`; no shipped `reconfigure.rhai` counterpart exists anywhere (see
    Handles).

Exposes:
  @Parameters — clap @Args struct deriving @Debug, @Serialize, @Deserialize; would
    mount on the commented @Commands::Reconfigure in ./mod.rs, so no live mount
    today; all ten fields module-private, reached only by the derives and @run.
  @run — @pub async fn @run(@args: @&@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>; the
    commented mod arm `reconfigure::run(args).await` already agrees with this
    signature — the revival blockers are the `format!` asymmetry and the @unwrap
    lint lane, not the call shape.

Accepts:
  @Parameters.namespace — `-n` / `--namespace`, env `NAMESPACE`, value name
    `NAMESPACE`, @String, required.
  @Parameters.instance — `-i` / `--instance`, env `INSTANCE`, value name
    `INSTANCE`, @String, required; names the CR to fetch, never validated here.
  @Parameters.vynil_namespace — `-v` / `--vynil-namespace`, env `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`,
    value name `VYNIL_NAMESPACE`, @String, required; reaches scripts only through
    `args`.
  @Parameters.package_dir — `-p` / `--package-dir`, env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, value
    name `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `/tmp/package`.
  @Parameters.script_dir — `-s` / `--script-dir`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `./agent/scripts`.
  @Parameters.template_dir — `-t` / `--template-dir`, env `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`,
    value name `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default
    `./agent/templates`; read by nothing in this Rust lane.
  @Parameters.agent_image — long-only `--agent-image`, env `AGENT_IMAGE`, value name
    `AGENT_IMAGE`, @String, clap default @common::DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE.
  @Parameters.tag — long-only `--tag`, env `TAG`, value name `TAG`, @String,
    required, forwarded verbatim in `args`, never parsed or validated as a version
    here.
  @Parameters.config_dir — `-c` / `--config-dir`, env `CONFIG_DIR`, value name
    `CONFIG_DIR`, @std::path::PathBuf, clap default `.`.
  @Parameters.controller_values — long-only `--controller-values`, env
    `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, value name `CONTROLLER_VALUES`, @String, clap default the
    two-character string `{}`.
  Implicit runtime preconditions frozen as in ./install.sdd: a live tokio
    multi-thread runtime for @set_tenant, and @common::context::init_k8s already
    called by @tenant::run (inert either way).

Returns:
  @Ok(@()) once the fixed snippet completes without a Rhai error — the snippet's
    @Dynamic is discarded by `let _ =` and never inspected.

Raises:
  Frozen-if-recompiled error surface — nothing raises today (the file never runs),
    and even a reconnected copy first trips the `format!` compile failure in Tasks
    before any of this can fire.
  @common::Error::KubeError from the `?` on the awaited @TenantInstance::get —
    missing @TenantInstance (`NotFound` mapped whole, never defaulted), wrong
    namespace, Forbidden — the first fallible step, nothing published when it fails.
  @common::Error::Core (wrapping the Rhai error, Display `Rhai script error:
    <rhai text>`) from the `?` on @Script::eval: snippet parse error, missing
    `context` or `reconfigure` import, or a thrown error inside either module.
  @std::panic! from @serde_json::to_value(args) followed by `@unwrap()` — a
    serialization failure aborts by panic instead of yielding
    @common::Error::SerializationError the way ./install.rs does; unreachable in
    practice through the derives. The workspace deny on product-code @unwrap bites
    this line at clap/clippy time once the file recompiles (see Tasks,
    /linting.sdd).
  The context-owned @panic! `cannot create the Kubernetes client: {e}` surfacing
    through @TenantInstance::get → @get_client_async with no resolvable cluster
    configuration.
  @set_tenant panics on a current-thread or absent runtime (contract in
    /common/src/context.sdd), not catchable by the `?` lanes.

Handles:
  Every @Err lane belongs to the commented mod arm — frozen @tracing::error line
    `Reconfiguring of a package failed with:` then @process::exit(6) per ./mod.sdd;
    this file logs nothing and never exits.
  No shipped `reconfigure.rhai` anywhere in /agent/scripts — default revival
    therefore dies at the second import unless the mounted package supplies
    `scripts/reconfigure.rhai`, the first search directory; `context` resolves from
    `/agent/scripts/tenant`.
  Eval failure after @set_tenant already ran — the process keeps the
    @VynilContext::TenantInstance variant for the remaining process lifetime (it
    ends in the exit-6).
  Rerun over a configured instance — no `status` branch here: both modules replay;
    any idempotence is script-side.
  Flags with no local reader (`vynil_namespace`, `tag`, `template_dir`,
    `agent_image`, `controller_values`) — their only observable use is the `args`
    JSON the scripts consume.

Must:
  Execute in this order with nothing between: build the interpreter, fetch the CR,
    publish context, inject `instance`, serialize and inject `args`, evaluate the
    snippet, return @Ok — the @run skeleton of ./install.rs verbatim except the two
    diffs named by the shape ancestor.
  Build the interpreter with @Script::new on exactly four resolver directories in
    this order: `{package_dir}/scripts`, `{config_dir}` (the bare directory),
    `{script_dir}/tenant`, `{script_dir}/lib` — path text interpolation giving the
    same strings as the twin's `@Path::display` sites, so a trailing `/` in a flag
    doubles the separator; earlier entries win an `import`.
  Fetch the CR with @TenantInstance::get on clones of @Parameters.namespace and
    @Parameters.instance — one namespaced named read, never a list, watch or
    create; an absent instance is an @Err, not a bootstrap path.
  Publish the fetched CR twice from the value and one clone: @set_tenant stores the
    clone as the process owner context and @rhai::Scope::set_value on @Script::ctx
    moves the original into the script variable named `instance`.
  Inject `args` as @Script::set_dynamic over @serde_json::to_value(args) — the
    object then carries exactly the ten snake_case keys `namespace`, `instance`,
    `vynil_namespace`, `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`,
    `tag`, `config_dir`, `controller_values` — @PathBuf values as path text,
    `agent_image` as a string, `controller_values` as a JSON string (its default
    renders `"{}"`, still a string).
  Evaluate the fixed four-statement snippet, nothing configurable in it, `context`
    first and `reconfigure` last:
      `import("context") as ctx;` `let context = ctx::run(instance, args);`
      `import("reconfigure") as reconfigure;` `reconfigure::run(instance, context);`
    — the map `ctx::run` returns becomes the second argument of
    `reconfigure::run`.
  Mutate nothing on the cluster itself: every write happens inside the Rhai modules
    through the registered @TenantInstance bridge; this lane reads the CR only.
  Emit no log and no stdout/stderr.

Must not:
  Branch on `status`, `tag` or `controller_values` in Rust: what reconfigure skips
    or replays is a script-side decision this lane never pre-empts.
  Render templates or apply manifests from Rust — `template_dir` steers no Rust
    code here, only the scripts through `args`.

Tasks:
  [ ] Decide revive vs delete: resurrect the commented triplet in ./mod.rs
      (`//mod reconfigure;`, the @Commands::Reconfigure variant, the exit-6 arm) or
      delete this file; the decision is shared with the matching tasks in ./mod.sdd
      and ./../service/reconfigure.sdd and must close in lockstep across all three.
  [ ] Untested: no test invokes @run — the file is never compiled, so none could;
      if revived, first cover every Scenario under the project TTD rule.
  [?] Twin compile asymmetry (frozen finding, verified): in hunk `@@ -78` the four
      `format!` sites at lines 81–84 pass the @PathBuf fields straight into `{}`,
      while the twin passes the `@Path::display` value. The premise that @PathBuf
      is Display-formattable is false: `PathBuf` implements no @std::fmt::Display
      (neither does @std::path::Path — which is why `@Path::display` exists), and
      rustc rejects all four sites with E0277 under both `edition 2021` and
      `edition 2024` (verified on rustc 1.97.1). So this copy does not compile
      identically to the twin —
      reconnected, lines 81–84 fail the build where the twin passes. Decide which
      twin's formatting is canonical before reviving either (adding `.display()`
      here restores parity).
  [?] @unwrap vs @map_err: serialization failure panics here where ./install.rs
      returns @common::Error::SerializationError; reconnected-and-compiling, the
      deny on product-code @unwrap in /linting.sdd turns this line into a hard
      clippy failure. Decide to normalize onto the install lane (or keep the
      panic, contradicting the workspace rule).
  [?] No shipped `reconfigure.rhai`: /agent/scripts carries `context.rhai` per kind
      but no reconfigure script for any kind, so revival is inert-with-an-import-
      error until either packages supply `scripts/reconfigure.rhai` (their
      entry-point pattern per /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.rs) or the agent
      ships one. Decide the supplier before the flag contract goes live.
  [?] Required-but-unread flags (`vynil_namespace`, `tag`) and the
      deserialization-less @Deserialize derive match ./install.rs exactly; revival
      inherits the open `[?]` set in ./install.sdd unchanged — resolve once there
      instead of duplicating.

Done when:
  The revive-or-delete decision is on record here, in ./mod.sdd and in the twin
    spec; if revived, the compile asymmetry and the @unwrap lane are decided away,
    every Scenario has a passing test, and clippy and fmt are green.

Scenario: revival trips the compile asymmetry before anything runs
  Given ./mod.rs revived verbatim — just the triplet uncommented, this source
    unchanged — and the twin kept as canonical formatting
  When cargo builds the agent crate
  Then four E0277 errors land at the `format!` sites on lines 81–84 (`PathBuf` not
    @std::fmt::Display), and the exit-6 wiring never links

Scenario: full run hands off in order with a package-supplied script
  Given all required flags supplied, an existing namespaced @TenantInstance, and
    `reconfigure.rhai` shipped by the mounted package under its `scripts` directory
    (the only default location it can resolve from)
  When @run is awaited
  Then @Script::new received the four search dirs `[package]/scripts`, `[config]`,
    `[script]/tenant`, `[script]/lib` in that order
  And before the eval @set_tenant published the tenant variant and `instance` and
    `args` are bound
  Then `ctx::run(instance, args)` executes before `reconfigure::run(instance,
    context)`, and the map it returns is exactly the second argument
    `reconfigure::run` receives
  And @run returns @Ok(()) whatever the discarded @Dynamic was

Scenario: args JSON equals the install ten keys at defaults
  Given a command line setting only the required flags
  When @run serializes @Parameters into `args`
  Then the object holds exactly the ten keys `namespace`, `instance`,
    `vynil_namespace`, `package_dir`, `script_dir`, `template_dir`, `agent_image`,
    `tag`, `config_dir`, `controller_values`
  And `controller_values` is the JSON string `"{}"`, `template_dir` is
    `./agent/templates` and `agent_image` is `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`

Scenario: missing CR fails before any handoff
  Given no @TenantInstance at that namespace/name — or its read is Forbidden
  When @run is awaited
  Then the `?` on @TenantInstance::get returns @Err(@common::Error::KubeError)
  And @set_tenant never ran, neither injection happened and the snippet never
    evaluated, so the exit-6 lane would log
    `Reconfiguring of a package failed with:` carrying the KubeError text

Scenario: default script tree cannot satisfy the reconfigure import
  Given a valid @TenantInstance, default `--script-dir` and a package directory
    holding no `reconfigure.rhai`
  When @run evaluates the snippet
  Then the `context` import succeeds and the `reconfigure` import fails,
    @Script::eval returns @Err(@common::Error::Core Display-prefixed
    `Rhai script error:`)
  And the process context already holds the tenant variant when the exit-6 log
    fires
